WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.399
Skills describe what an agent can do, and entitlements decide where an agent may work.

00:00:06.399 --> 00:00:10.448
This video shows why they exist, how to create a skill, and how

00:00:10.448 --> 00:00:13.500
to give an agent queues, campaigns and skills.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:20.863
Not every agent can help every customer.

00:00:20.863 --> 00:00:25.427
A customer who speaks Spanish needs an agent who speaks Spanish, and a

00:00:25.427 --> 00:00:28.730
billing question needs someone who knows billing.

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:35.523
A skill describes what an agent can do, such as Spanish, Billing, or Tier 2 support.

00:00:35.523 --> 00:00:38.410
A queue can require or prefer skills.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:44.140
An entitlement record decides which queues and campaigns one agent may sign in

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:49.120
to, in what order the agent is offered work, and which skills the agent holds.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:55.830
Skills are created once, in a list.

00:00:55.830 --> 00:01:00.300
They come with the work distribution feature of the Contact Center.

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:03.765
Each agent has one entitlement record:

00:01:03.765 --> 00:01:08.947
allowed queues with a priority and a delay, allowed campaigns, and skills with

00:01:08.947 --> 00:01:11.230
a proficiency from one to five.

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:14.764
Entitlements are a feature you turn on.

00:01:14.764 --> 00:01:19.032
Without it, any agent may sign in to any queue or campaign, and

00:01:19.032 --> 00:01:21.940
there is no screen to give agents skills.

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:29.623
Open Interaction Center, Management, Skills.

00:01:29.623 --> 00:01:32.532
The list shows the skills that exist.

00:01:32.532 --> 00:01:34.020
Click Add Skill.

00:01:34.583 --> 00:01:39.643
Enter a Name, such as Tier 2 support, and an optional Description.

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:43.922
Leave Enabled ticked and click Save.

00:01:43.922 --> 00:01:48.278
A disabled skill stays on the agents and queues that already use it,

00:01:48.278 --> 00:01:50.810
but it cannot be picked for new ones.

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:59.650
Open Agent entitlements, and click Add agent entitlements.

00:02:00.126 --> 00:02:04.820
Click Browse users, search for the person, and pick them as the User.

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:10.516
Each user has one entitlement record, and the screen tells you if one already exists.

00:02:10.966 --> 00:02:15.500
Under Allowed queues, pick every queue the agent may sign in to.

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:19.386
Removing a queue later also signs the agent out of it.

00:02:19.836 --> 00:02:22.639
Queue preferences list the allowed queues.

00:02:22.639 --> 00:02:25.325
A lower Priority number is served first.

00:02:25.325 --> 00:02:29.879
Delay makes a caller wait that many seconds before this agent is offered

00:02:29.879 --> 00:02:32.506
work, so the agent can back up a queue.

00:02:36.708 --> 00:02:41.500
Under Allowed campaigns, pick the dialer campaigns the agent may work.

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:43.328
This site has none yet.

00:02:43.786 --> 00:02:47.366
Under Skills, click Add skill, and pick a skill.

00:02:47.822 --> 00:02:51.670
Set its Proficiency from 1, basic, to 5, expert.

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:57.086
A queue that requires a skill at a minimum proficiency only offers its

00:02:57.086 --> 00:02:59.652
work to agents at or above it.

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:01.164
Click Save.

00:03:01.164 --> 00:03:06.930
The agent can now sign in to these queues, and receives work that matches their skills.

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:15.775
The list shows how many queues and campaigns each agent is allowed.

00:03:15.775 --> 00:03:17.549
Edit changes a record.

00:03:17.549 --> 00:03:20.336
Entitlement records cannot be deleted:

00:03:20.336 --> 00:03:23.250
remove the queues and campaigns instead.

00:03:23.743 --> 00:03:25.912
Supervisors need a record too.

00:03:25.912 --> 00:03:30.913
The Live dashboard and the shared voicemail show a supervisor only the queues

00:03:30.913 --> 00:03:35.793
and campaigns on their own record, so without one their dashboard is empty.

00:03:39.993 --> 00:03:44.693
A Spanish queue that only offers work to agents with the Spanish skill.

00:03:45.443 --> 00:03:49.576
A backup agent, with a delay on the sales queue, who helps only

00:03:49.576 --> 00:03:51.613
when the sales team is busy.

00:03:52.363 --> 00:03:57.953
A senior agent with Tier 2 support at proficiency 5, for the hardest questions.

00:03:58.703 --> 00:04:04.393
A supervisor with a record for the queues they supervise, so the dashboard shows their team.

00:04:06.393 --> 00:04:11.338
Create the skills, give every agent an entitlement record, and work reaches the

00:04:11.338 --> 00:04:12.851
people who can help.

00:04:12.851 --> 00:04:14.363
Thanks for watching.

